# CO-WP-ARCHITECTURE-UPDATE-001 — Roadmap Alignment

Status: **PRODUCT OWNER ARCHITECTURE DIRECTION**  
**Implementation Status: DO NOT IMPLEMENT**  
Purpose: Roadmap alignment only — no code, no module start, no Business work.

## Architectural update

After Product Owner review, the Wealth Partner App roadmap matured beyond the original plan.

This is an **architecture update only**. **No implementation is authorised.**

## Important change

Although **Home** is functionally complete and awaiting Product Owner certification, the next engineering priority will **NOT** automatically be the **Business** module.

A new Enterprise module must be **designed** before Business implementation begins.

## New Enterprise module

| | |
|--|--|
| **Name** | Enterprise Experience Engine (**EEE**) |
| **Location** | **Catalyst One** |
| **Not** | Wealth Partner App |

### Purpose

EEE becomes the publishing and experience orchestration layer for the entire Rupee Catalyst ecosystem.

The Wealth Partner App **never owns business content**.  
It **renders** Enterprise Experiences created inside Catalyst One.

### EEE will eventually control

Hero Carousel · Recommended Actions · Today’s Highlights · Business Feed · Notifications · Personalised Greetings · Campaigns · Training · Marketing Creatives · Product Workspaces · Digital Toolkit · Recognition · CEO Messages · Festival Messages · Future Enterprise Experiences

## Product Workspace (constitutional)

Every financial product eventually opens into an **Enterprise Product Workspace**.

Examples: Home Loan · LAP · Business Loan · Mutual Fund · Insurance · Fixed Deposit · future products.

**Never hardcode product pages** in the Wealth Partner App.

Catalyst One owns: Banner · Description · Product Benefits · Documents · Lenders · Interest Rates · Marketing · Training · Calculators · FAQs · CTA.

The app renders.

## Partner Entitlements

Product availability is managed **entirely from Catalyst One**.

Examples: Loans · Mutual Funds · Insurance · Fixed Deposits · Bonds · PMS · AIF.

Every Wealth Partner has **configurable product access**.  
The app must **never hardcode product visibility**.

## Partner Tier Engine

Partner Tier is **NOT** manually assigned.

Tier is calculated automatically from **configurable product-wise targets** assigned during onboarding.

Targets may differ by: City · Product Specialisation · Partner Type · Business Model.

Catalyst One calculates: Product Achievement · Overall Achievement · Tier · Progress.

The Wealth Partner App **only displays** the results.

## Next design activity

Before Business Module implementation begins, Product Owner intends to **design the Enterprise Experience Engine architecture**.

- Do **not** begin implementing EEE.  
- Do **not** modify Business.  
- Treat this as the **updated Enterprise roadmap** only.  
- Await further Product Owner instructions before the next implementation phase.

